From 20611d4e19fd738cb693bdede60d65548c05a54f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phxinyang <phxinyang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:58:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: deblocking filter controls for HFI gen2

Add the strongtz/libva-v4l2 patch 0003 (Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>),
rebased onto ianchb/sm8550-mainline sheng-7.2.6 (42f3b40c702a).

Iris does not expose deblocking filter controls for HFI gen2 encoder
sessions, leaving applications unable to configure the filter mode or its
offsets.

Expose the standard V4L2 H.264 loop filter mode, alpha and beta controls
and the HEVC loop filter mode, tc and beta controls. Register them in the
gen2 encoder capability table with filtering enabled and zero offsets by
default, and reject changes once OUTPUT is streaming.

Translate the codec-specific mode enums and pack the offsets, biased by
six, into HFI_PROP_DEBLOCKING_MODE. Only send the controls for the active
codec so that the other codec's settings cannot overwrite them.

sheng-7.2.6 has a single gen2 encoder table and no milos_enc array, so
the upstream patch's second table block is not part of this rebase; the
six entries were inserted after ENTROPY_MODE in inst_fw_cap_sm8550_enc.
